# Proposed (milestone2.md, "BallVector", "Values"): the constructor of a BallVector of one limb from
# the program's centers and radius. A ball vector (architecture.md, "Ball vectors"): each center
# guarded and written; the state of norm_upper_1 on the centers written; the radius the guarded radius,
# a NaN when a center is infinite (bv_make_radius); the finish norm_finish_1 under the mask that no
# center was a NaN and the radius is not negative (bv_make_finish). So a radius that is negative or a
# NaN, or +infinity, or a center that is not finite, gives the whole space; otherwise the centers and
# the radius are those given, exactly (a zero made positive). Its claim would be a new kind,
# makes_ball_vector (ballvector.py, B1 to B3); not in gen/kernels: the page gives no listing, and the
# finish's claim needs a field the vocabulary has not (bv_make_finish.kernel).
fold:          bv_make_1
arrays:        supplied c
scalars:       supplied r
state:         m, mask ok
step:          z = bv_center_entry_1(c)
record:        (m, ok) = norm_step_1(m, ok, z)
combine:       (m, ok) = norm_combine(m, ok, m, ok)
radius:        rz = bv_make_radius(m, r)
finish:        (rr, finite) = bv_make_finish(rz, ok)
orders:        sequential, lanes
writes:        z
output:        rr
output:        mask finite
value:         c
min_precision: 1
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
